15- Which development model or combination of models would you choose—Scrum, XP, FDD, RUP, Spiral, or another approach? Justify your choice and explain how your team would organize the development process.
Answer 15: We'd go with Scrum here, maybe mixed with some XP practices on the technical side.
Scrum fits because it's built exactly for this: regular demos happen through Sprint Reviews, delivery is incremental since every sprint ends with a shippable increment, and the backlog gets re-prioritized each sprint instead of being locked in from the start like with RUP or Waterfall.
Since it's a big system, throwing in XP stuff like continuous integration and test-driven development would help keep the code from turning into a mess as it grows.
Team-wise: a Product Owner handling the backlog based on customer feedback, a Scrum Master keeping the sprints on track, and developers using CI/TDD so technical debt doesn't pile up. RUP or Spiral would fit worse since they're more predictive and don't handle constantly changing requirements as well as Scrum does.
